& [FixtureAuthority]
  + commit compact canonical UTF-8 JSON request bytes for one lifecycle-valid case and one structurally admitted lifecycle-refused case
  + bind each fixture to stable fixture identity byte length SHA256 expected exact Slice7 response digest and source builder reference in a separate SOP manifest
  + generation is an explicit maintenance operation and ordinary tests are read-only snapshot equality checks
  + deterministic signing keys and asserted facts are fixtures only and confer no production trust or effect authority

& [McpExperimentBridge]
  + create an experiment-only Rust harness that launches the closed Slice8 and Slice10 stdio binaries through official rmcp client transport
  + Arm A sends the complete governed request to Slice8 for every validation
  + Arm B registers the complete governed request once outside measured steady state then sends only the exact compact Slice10 handle for every validation
  + both arms decode structuredContent into the same NativeLifecycleValidationResponse and compare canonical bytes to the direct Slice7 result
  + subprocess start exit timeout protocol malformed response and semantic mismatch are explicit bounded faults

& [InferenceCheckpointFlow]
  + reuse the pinned unmodified llama.cpp OpenAI-compatible two-checkpoint flow in experiments/llama_tool_reflection
  + checkpoint one requires exactly one selected lifecycle validation tool call with parallel calls disabled
  + the host closes tool name and argument schema then dispatches the selected arm
  + the tool result is appended with the exact originating tool_call_id
  + checkpoint two uses tool_choice none and returns only a closed bounded projection of source identity operation lifecycle outcome stage and disposition
  + the host verifies projection import against its authoritative typed lifecycle response

& [Preflight]
  + live execution requires an observed healthy local endpoint pinned provider release accessible model identity and recorded generation settings
  + absence or mismatch performs no live call and yields provider_unavailable or provider_mismatch rather than synthetic measurements
  + provider installation remote fallback model download and host-policy changes are not authorized

& [Measurement]
  + use identical fixture prompt provider model generation settings timeout and bounded trial count across arms
  + preserve raw warmup and measured trials with arm order request bytes response bytes prompt tokens completion tokens wall latency tool-call validity import validity and exact response equality
  + report first-call and steady-state latency separately
  + report transport compression and model-context token differences separately
  + retain invalid refused timeout and incomplete trials and exclude only declared warmups and restart trials from steady-state aggregates

& [AdversarialClosure]
  + missing changed malformed unknown-field and response-divergent fixtures refuse before provider traffic
  + unknown tool method command field duplicate parallel call malformed call substituted handle and mismatched tool_call_id refuse visibly
  + a compact handle refuses after Slice10 process restart and restart trials never imply persistence
  + valid and lifecycle-refused cases must both preserve exact core outcomes through each completed arm

& [BoundsAndEffects]
  + model-facing schemas diagnostics projections transcript retention and result files have explicit byte or item ceilings
  + no model-private reasoning hidden state KV cache secret credential unrelated prompt or retained request-body inspection enters results
  + no filesystem build signing admission installation deployment remote machine FPGA or production runner operation is exposed as a model tool

& [Acceptance]
  + governed fixtures regenerate identically and snapshot tests establish strict JSON and exact direct response digests
  + direct and official-client stateless and custody bridge tests pass for valid refused malformed substituted duplicate and restart paths
  + provider-independent harness tests pass without a live model
  + when preflight passes both live arms complete comparable trials and raw evidence recomputes every published result
  + focused debug optimized release lint format evidence and repository-diff gates pass

& [NonGoals]
  + llama.cpp source modification mid-token insertion shared hidden state KV-cache exchange remote provider remote machine persistent custody production authorization generalized orchestration FPGA OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft

